# Day 9 — Classes & OOP Fundamentals

Before we start, an important point:

> Modern React Native primarily uses Functional Components and Hooks, not Classes.

However, you still need to learn OOP because:

* React Native legacy projects use Class Components.
* iOS (Swift) and Android (Kotlin/Java) are OOP-heavy.
* Many design patterns are OOP-based.
* Interviews often ask OOP questions.
* Understanding classes makes inheritance easier.

---

# What is OOP?

OOP = Object-Oriented Programming

Think:

```text
Real World Entity
      ↓
Object
      ↓
Properties + Behavior
```

Example:

```text
Car
 ├─ brand
 ├─ color
 ├─ speed
 ├─ start()
 └─ stop()
```

In JavaScript:

```javascript
const car = {
   brand: "BMW",
   color: "Black",

   start() {
      console.log("Car Started");
   }
};
```

