# Class vs Object

Most asked interview question.

---

## Class

A class is a blueprint.

Example:

```text
House Blueprint
```

Not an actual house.

---

## Object

An object is a real instance created from a class.

Example:

```text
Actual House
```

---

Visual:

```text
Class
   ↓
Create Object
   ↓
Object
```

---

# Creating a Class

Syntax:

```javascript
class User {

}
```

Example:

```javascript
class User {

}
```

This class currently does nothing.

---

# Creating an Object

Use:

```javascript
new
```

Example:

```javascript
class User {

}

const user1 = new User();
```

Now:

```text
user1
```

is an object.

---

# Constructor

The constructor runs automatically when object is created.

Syntax:

```javascript
constructor() {

}
```

Example:

```javascript
class User {

   constructor() {
      console.log("User Created");
   }

}

const user1 = new User();
```

Output:

```text
User Created
```

---

# Why Constructor?

To initialize object properties.

Example:

```javascript
class User {

   constructor(name) {
      this.name = name;
   }

}
```

Create object:

```javascript
const user1 =
 new User("Siddharth");
```

Now:

```javascript
console.log(user1.name);
```

Output:

```text
Siddharth
```

---

# Understanding this

This is extremely important.

Inside class:

```javascript
this
```

means:

```text
Current Object
```

Example:

```javascript
class User {

   constructor(name) {
      this.name = name;
   }

}
```

When:

```javascript
const user1 =
 new User("Siddharth");
```

Internally:

```javascript
user1.name = "Siddharth";
```

---

# Visual

```text
user1
 │
 └── name = Siddharth
```

---

# Multiple Properties

Example:

```javascript
class User {

   constructor(name, age) {

      this.name = name;
      this.age = age;
   }

}
```

Create:

```javascript
const user1 =
 new User("Siddharth",30);
```

Output:

```javascript
console.log(user1);
```

```javascript
{
  name:"Siddharth",
  age:30
}
```

